      "weather": "Fine",
      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "There was plenty to like about last week's performance of OHOKA COBRA NZ (1) when he came from a wider barrier to place. He is much better served by this barrier having led from there to win over this distance two back at Newcastle. He could do that again. JILLIBY FABIO (4) worked to the front from one spot wider than this and kept going to score by 5.5m at this circuit and distance last start. This looks another suitable assignment so he could back that up. Manners have let ROCKNROLL COWBOY (2) down in his two outings since he kicked off his campaign with two wins at this circuit and distance. Has won a trial since the last appearance and draws well. He is good enough to win if he gets it right. AGATHA BLOOM (12) may need luck from the outside draw but is going well with wins in three of her last five outings, one of them from this barrier. VAN BASTEN (6) hasn't been far away of late and draws lower than last time.",
